sequenceDiagram
    participant GateA as eFTI Gate A (eu-ee31)
    participant GateB as eFTI Gate B (eu-fi01)
    participant CA as Trusted CA Bundle

    Note over GateA,GateB: Gate-to-gate fast protocol — mTLS<br/>Replaces eDelivery AS4 envelope for low-latency intra-network calls.<br/>Both endpoints present X.509 client certificates.

    GateA->>GateA: Load client cert + private key<br/>from K8s Secret (mounted at runtime)
    GateA->>GateB: POST /services/fast<br/>Client cert: CN=gate-eu-ee31.efti.ee<br/>X-Request-ID: 7c9e6679-...

    GateB->>CA: Verify client cert chain<br/>against trusted-cas.pem (configured per gate)
    alt cert valid + CN matches a registered gate
        CA-->>GateB: Trust chain OK
        GateB->>GateB: Resolve gate by cert CN<br/>SELECT id FROM gates WHERE eDeliveryCert = <cert PEM>
        GateB->>GateB: Authorize: gate is ONLINE<br/>Apply rate limit per gate
        GateB-->>GateA: 200 OK<br/>application/json — search results / dataset / follow-up
        GateB->>GateB: INSERT INTO audit_log (action='g2g_request', resource='gate', resource_id=<cert CN>, recorded_at=NOW())
    else cert invalid or CN not registered
        CA-->>GateB: Untrusted / chain incomplete
        GateB-->>GateA: 401 Unauthorized<br/>application/problem+json<br/>code: UNAUTHORIZED
        GateB->>GateB: INSERT INTO audit_log (action='g2g_request_denied', resource='gate', details={reason})
    end

    Note over GateA,GateB: X-API-Key header is NEVER accepted on /services/fast.<br/>Plain bearer auth is rejected — only mTLS satisfies this endpoint.
